any-of: IAC-DOCKER-LATEST_TAG-01
any-of: IAC-DOCKER-UNPINNED_DIGEST-01
correlate-on: file
tags: derived
remediation: The Dockerfile's own base image reference is not pinned to an
  immutable tag and content digest, and the built image already carries a
  Debian/Ubuntu package with a known, published advisory - the two are
  connected: an unpinned base is exactly what lets a routine rebuild
  silently reintroduce a vulnerable version instead of refreshing it away.
  Pin the base image with an explicit release tag AND an `@sha256:...`
  digest (IAC-DOCKER-UNPINNED_DIGEST-01's own remediation), then rebuild
  against a current base and re-scan to confirm the advisory clears.
references: CWE-1104
references: CWE-829
references: https://owasp.org/Top10/A06_2021-Vulnerable_and_Outdated_Components/

